{"city":{"id":"fushimi-inari","name":"Fushimi Inari","country":"Japan","country_code":"JP","timezone":"Asia/Tokyo","locale":"en-JP","description":"Fushimi Inari Taisha, the shrine of the rice god: through the great vermilion Romon, past the fox guardians, and up Mount Inari under thousands of torii to Yotsutsuji and the summit.","vertical_datum":"m T.P. (Tokyo Peil)","year":2026,"tour":[{"title":"The mountain of the rice god","text":"For thirteen centuries merchants and farmers have climbed Inari-yama to pray for a good harvest and a good year. Thousands of torii line the paths to the 233 m summit, every one a gift.","cam":[-1100,-500,420],"tgt":[0,120,80],"date":[11,20],"from":"15:00","to":"16:00","hold":8},{"title":"The Romon","text":"Toyotomi Hideyoshi's gate of 1589, about 14 m of vermilion under hinoki bark. Inari's foxes stand guard before it: one holds a jewel, the other the key to the rice granary.","cam":[-440,110,50],"tgt":[-397,125,47],"date":[11,20],"from":"15:30","to":"16:20","hold":8},{"title":"Senbon Torii","text":"Two tunnels of torii side by side, close enough to touch, glowing orange when the low sun comes through. Walk round to the back of each gate: the names are the people and companies who gave it.","cam":[-270,40,70],"tgt":[-175,70,52],"date":[11,20],"from":"16:00","to":"16:40","hold":8}],"start":{"date":[11,20],"time":"15:40","cam":[-1100,-500,420],"tgt":[0,120,80]},"protection":{"title":"No statutory sun rule for public places","summary":"Kyoto protects its skyline with height limits (a cap of 31 m in the busiest districts) and Japan limits shadows on homes with the Building Standards Act, but neither protects sun on parks. Sun on these places is measured for information, not tested against a rule.","source_note":"No legal window is transcribed for these places, so each is shown for 10:00-14:00 and none is marked protected.","reading_note":"Heights come from Project PLATEAU, measured from aerial survey in 2020-2021, so buildings finished since are missing or low.","default_time_basis":"clock","tip":"Tip: the hillside puts the lanes in shade early on winter afternoons.","unprotected_label":"no rule"},"minor_labels":[],"place_labels":[],"sun_hours_region":[-1080,1080,-650,650],"lat":34.966,"lon":135.777,"architecture":"japan","signage":0.3,"arrivals":{"Inari-yama \u7a32\u8377\u5c71 233 m":{"at":[797,138]},"Senbon Torii \u5343\u672c\u9ce5\u5c45":{"at":[-204.2,107.3],"look":[-195.5,99.0]}}},"frame":{"proj":"+proj=tmerc +lat_0=34.966 +lon_0=135.777 +k=1 +x_0=0 +y_0=0 +ellps=WGS84 +units=m +no_defs","lon0":135.777,"lat0":34.966,"x":[-1090,1090],"y":[-660,660],"units":"m, z = m T.P. (Tokyo Peil)"},"terrain":{"file":"terrain.json","nx":219,"ny":133,"cell":10.0,"scale":0.1,"origin":"north-west, row-major, rows go south","bare_earth":true},"ground":[{"file":"ground_0_0.jpg","x0":-1090.0,"x1":-90.0,"y0":-540.0,"y1":660.0,"avif":"ground_0_0.avif"},{"file":"ground_1_0.jpg","x0":-90.0,"x1":910.0,"y0":-540.0,"y1":660.0,"avif":"ground_1_0.avif"},{"file":"ground_2_0.jpg","x0":910.0,"x1":1910.0,"y0":-540.0,"y1":660.0,"avif":"ground_2_0.avif"},{"file":"ground_0_1.jpg","x0":-1090.0,"x1":-90.0,"y0":-1740.0,"y1":-540.0,"avif":"ground_0_1.avif"},{"file":"ground_1_1.jpg","x0":-90.0,"x1":910.0,"y0":-1740.0,"y1":-540.0,"avif":"ground_1_1.avif"},{"file":"ground_2_1.jpg","x0":910.0,"x1":1910.0,"y0":-1740.0,"y1":-540.0,"avif":"ground_2_1.avif"}],"shore":{"file":"shore.png","cell":2.5,"nx":872,"ny":528,"x0":-1090,"y1":660,"encoding":"r: 128 + 2 x signed distance to the shoreline (m, water positive); g: sand; b: rock","slopes":{"sand":0.04,"rock":0.25,"built":1.0},"floor_m":4.0,"sand_polygons":0,"rock_polygons":2},"water":{},"trees":{"mix":{"zelkova":0.2,"ginkgo":0.14,"camphor":0.16,"cherry":0.12,"maple":0.12,"pine":0.1,"evergreen":0.16},"woods":{"sugi":0.42,"evergreen":0.37,"camphor":0.08,"maple":0.03,"pine":0.05,"zelkova":0.05},"note":"Species are not mapped; the mix is a guess from Kyoto's street-tree surveys and the shrine's own